@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts its positional objects with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``.
+
+It does not pretty-print, wrap, crop, apply markup, or replace emoji codes. Containers are written as their string form, and text such as ``[bold]`` or ``:smile:`` is written literally.
+
+Highlighting is applied by default; pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=True`` to force it. A basic ``style`` can also be applied::
+
+    >>> console.out("[1, 2]", "foo", sep=" | ", style="bold")
+
+
